{
  "_": "The weekly burndown's rule (docs/hub/usage.md, \"The weekly burndown\"): typed readings to each bucket's percent, pace and gap, and the reading's cache line. One row per case. Every instant is UTC; the week is weekStart to weekEnd. Per bucket the latest reading at or after weekStart, before weekEnd and at or before now that names it (a tie goes to the machine that sorts last); pace = floor(elapsed at the reading / week length x 100 + 0.5); gap = percent - pace; cachedAt = the latest reading used; renewsAt = cachedAt + cacheHours; due = now >= renewsAt. Asserted by Tests/Test-Burn.ps1 through Get-P20Burndown (Scripts/Read-BurnReadings.ps1); the web asserts it where it draws the burndown.",
  "weekStart": "2026-11-06T13:00:00.000Z",
  "weekEnd": "2026-11-13T13:00:00.000Z",
  "buckets": [
    {
      "key": "general",
      "label": "General"
    },
    {
      "key": "premium",
      "label": "Premium (Fable)"
    }
  ],
  "cases": [
